{"title":"2015 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be non-zero digits, so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> is a two-digit positive integer and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> is a three-digit positive integer made up of the digits <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Suppose that\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/f/e7f97f7880cdb68c9a2ce17f61a52036722569e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\begin{array}{cccc} &amp;&amp;\\!\\!B\\!\\!&amp;\\!\\!C\\!\\!\\\\ &amp;\\!\\!A\\!\\!&amp;\\!\\!B\\!\\!&amp;\\!\\!C\\!\\!\\\\ +&amp;\\!A\\!\\!&amp;\\!\\!B\\!\\!&amp;\\!\\!C\\!\\!\\\\ \\hline &amp;\\!8\\!\\!&amp;\\!\\!7\\!\\!&amp;\\!\\!6\\!\\! \\end{array}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -36px\" width=\"92\" height=\"82\" /></center>\n<p>What is the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/c/61c5c96b5fc71513978687cb5076d21f4536d05f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A + B + C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"87\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/3/c532ffabd8059b3f068983ef1c257952e8207367.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" /> must sum up to a number ending in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. The largest possible sum for three digits is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/f/6ff2ae475e662eb83e408487daa5688a343d18bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9 \\times 3 = 27$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> represents a digit, so this must be either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/a/bda00d9a38a0c6bd9aac2512c6d065581882d43c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$26$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is an integer, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/3/c532ffabd8059b3f068983ef1c257952e8207367.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" /> must also be an integer, so the only possibility that works out of these is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. This means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/8/3a8bd3ec69779ce02795562ac358029a86b66426.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C = \\frac{6}{3} = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"87\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_2&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Next, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/9/cb93b9dbd8a783496111be0f383d889cf5aebfb4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3B$\" width=\"23\" height=\"12\" /> must end in a number ending in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Since there was no carry over, the largest possible sum remains the same, so the possibilities are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b7616a230c77f0d9a577e5bca01aa06f1c35c457.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/5/1051e7d41ec0b8bd688a872be17538413f4ee97b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$27$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is an integer, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/9/cb93b9dbd8a783496111be0f383d889cf5aebfb4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3B$\" width=\"23\" height=\"12\" /> must also be an integer. This means that the only possibility that works out of these three is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/5/1051e7d41ec0b8bd688a872be17538413f4ee97b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$27$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, which occurs when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/f/02ff553120bb573098979aba967d6522952259e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B = \\frac{27}{3} = 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"96\" height=\"38\" />. We then carry over the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to the hundreds place.\n</p><p>Next, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/d/70d96986d8eeda33a6dc2cc02251b2e37d681b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2A + 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"56\" height=\"16\" /> must end in a number ending in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/b/98b9116007a90d8b496b3a9aa7920304e0d94a85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2A$\" width=\"22\" height=\"13\" /> must end in a number ending in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. However, there is no carry-over to the thousands place, so the only possible value here is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. This means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/f/74f1a6c87a39f85f1a8191d2628b777a4802f6cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = \\frac{6}{2} = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"86\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>The sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/d/d8d52081a624958b97ac58b05ee53943c55e8872.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 + 9 + 2 = 12 + 2 = \\boxed{14}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"201\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Verifying_A.2C_B.2C_and_C\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Verifying_A,_B,_and_C\">Verifying A, B, and C</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Verifying A, B, and C\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/0/f80d2fd9de35bd48dc77bf50405b4ff46a2de796.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = 3$\" width=\"46\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89f66000f7352070c8e261653d8293bd264af2e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B = 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/d/13d38e76d7d5fcfc00ea546b2219585c058823e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C = 2$\" width=\"47\" height=\"12\" />, then the sum in the original problem is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/5/565baf4f361e1734aca4e8d68df165aa3532a91b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$392 + 392 + 92 = 784 + 92 = 876$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"262\" height=\"15\" />. This matches the actual expected sum, so we have verified that our values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are correct.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CSMC\" title=\"2015 CSMC\">2015 CSMC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CSMC_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2015 CSMC Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CSMC_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2015 CSMC Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_1\" title=\"2015 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 1\">Part A Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2015 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 3 (page does not exist)\">Part A Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_1\" title=\"2015 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 1\">Part A 1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Part A 2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2015 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 3 (page does not exist)\">Part A 3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_4\" title=\"2015 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 4\">Part A 4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_5\" title=\"2015 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 5\">Part A 5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2015 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 6 (page does not exist)\">Part A 6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2015 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 1 (page does not exist)\">Part B 1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2015 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 2 (page does not exist)\">Part B 2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2015 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 3 (page does not exist)\">Part B 3</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=CEMC_Senior_Competition\" title=\"CEMC Senior Competition\">CEMC Senior Competition</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018060745\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.032 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.053 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 297/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1693/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 134/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8444/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   16.760      1 -total\n 43.02%    7.211      1 Template:CEMC_CIMC/CSMC_box\n 37.05%    6.209      1 Template:Image_needed\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:37301:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018060745 and revision id 287960. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}